WEBVTT

00:05.980 --> 00:08.410
Have you seen Tom lately?

00:08.410 --> 00:10.250
Nope, I haven't.

00:11.980 --> 00:14.440
Jimmy and Norton are missing, too.

00:14.950 --> 00:17.450
Hope they aren't getting beat up somewhere.

00:17.450 --> 00:18.230
Scary thought.

00:20.170 --> 00:23.610
They might have keeled over 
and died in the cold.

00:45.320 --> 00:46.560
<i>Philomela...</i>

02:29.150 --> 02:32.210
Welcoming your father and mother, huh?

02:32.570 --> 02:33.900
I see.

02:33.900 --> 02:39.290
More sinful than Orpheus, who traveled 
to the underworld to seek his wife.

02:42.660 --> 02:47.970
You did that to yourself just 
to bring back the dead?

02:48.470 --> 02:49.340
Yes.

02:49.340 --> 02:51.150
That's right.

02:51.150 --> 02:55.750
So I'd like you to stop 
closing off the College.

02:56.520 --> 02:59.200
That's my only wish.

02:59.800 --> 03:04.190
You wouldn't want to end up with 
people who are as dried out

03:04.580 --> 03:10.010
and lifeless as a pouch of 
forgotten potpourri, would you?

03:13.200 --> 03:14.010
Philomela!

03:16.150 --> 03:17.680
Stay out!

03:28.140 --> 03:29.920
The amulet!

03:32.830 --> 03:35.450
<i>Even though she's changed form, I can tell.</i>

03:36.320 --> 03:37.580
That's Philomela.

03:38.270 --> 03:40.760
Philomela Sargant.

03:40.760 --> 03:41.810
<i>That's</i> her?

03:46.720 --> 03:50.120
<i>She's begun corrupting the instructors, too.</i>

03:50.120 --> 03:52.700
<i>She passes through even mental defenses.</i>

03:53.500 --> 03:55.970
<i>There must be a god inside that thing.</i>

03:56.770 --> 03:59.760
Principal, I'm pleading with you...

04:00.150 --> 04:03.960
Open the College. Please?

04:07.980 --> 04:09.270
Florence.

04:30.480 --> 04:32.400
Thank you very much.

04:33.140 --> 04:36.330
Well, with that...

04:40.420 --> 04:42.280
Follower of the moon,

04:42.920 --> 04:48.920
incarnate of the moon, one 
who bears unwanted pity...

04:49.640 --> 04:53.760
Sing your rage. Sing your hatred!

04:54.090 --> 04:55.150
Philome—

04:55.930 --> 04:56.850
No.

05:15.330 --> 05:18.160
Alcyone...?

05:19.210 --> 05:22.040
Lady Philomela...

05:33.930 --> 05:35.570
A werewolf!

06:13.640 --> 06:15.630
Give us a hand if you aren't injured!

06:17.840 --> 06:19.380
Would you happen to know?

06:22.720 --> 06:24.160
You all right?

06:32.260 --> 06:33.960
I don't think you can get up yet.

06:34.440 --> 06:36.780
Stay put until your magic power comes back.

06:36.780 --> 06:39.340
I'm gonna go help out.

06:43.690 --> 06:44.620
Shit.

06:45.540 --> 06:47.640
I trust there are none dead.

06:48.360 --> 06:50.950
Go help in the nurse's office.

06:51.460 --> 06:52.500
Principal.

06:53.650 --> 06:57.030
Ah, you kids are safe.

06:57.030 --> 06:57.770
Thank goodness.

06:58.130 --> 07:00.100
We're going after them.

07:00.100 --> 07:02.320
I agree. We need to chase them.

07:02.320 --> 07:04.190
Forget it.

07:04.810 --> 07:10.510
She's clearly been far too corrupted 
by the resident of the magic book.

07:12.150 --> 07:15.560
She's beginning to lose her humanity.

07:17.950 --> 07:22.590
Her body and mind will soon 
fail, and she'll be done.

07:23.570 --> 07:26.990
So it was all right to kill her?

07:27.720 --> 07:30.570
I understand you were never intent 
on trying to hold her down.

07:32.720 --> 07:35.970
I'm responsible for this College.

07:36.460 --> 07:41.730
I must prioritize the health and 
safety of the staff and students.

07:43.240 --> 07:45.730
It isn't prudent to spend time on someone

07:46.190 --> 07:49.360
who's well aware that 
she's destroying herself.

07:50.010 --> 07:51.660
Unless, that is...

07:51.660 --> 07:58.400
You're suggesting I should have placed 
everyone's lives on the line to save her alone?

08:00.570 --> 08:01.920
Well...

08:01.920 --> 08:05.310
Or do you think you could 
have done something?

08:05.810 --> 08:10.580
Perhaps your courage has helped you 
through many past ordeals.

08:11.110 --> 08:16.270
If the result of that is that arm of yours, 
I can only conclude that you are a fool.

08:18.940 --> 08:23.450
Chise Hatori, if you truly 
want to protect your friends,

08:25.140 --> 08:31.500
you'll have to put away your pathetic, 
self-congratulatory sense of compassion.

08:40.680 --> 08:41.500
<i>I know...</i>

08:43.580 --> 08:46.090
<i>I know I have to hold back.</i>

08:47.470 --> 08:50.210
<i>I know I'm just doing it to satisfy myself.</i>

08:52.370 --> 08:53.570
<i>But...</i>

08:56.000 --> 09:00.320
<i>If I hold back now, she'll die!</i>

09:10.410 --> 09:11.390
Good on you.

09:15.460 --> 09:17.450
E-Elias?

09:18.390 --> 09:21.830
You would normally have darted off by now.

09:22.700 --> 09:28.170
I hear that when a puppy learns 
to <i>stay</i>, it needs to be rewarded.

09:29.200 --> 09:30.940
R-Right...

09:31.780 --> 09:33.500
Ainsworth?

09:35.050 --> 09:39.230
The College is a place that 
raises prospective sorcerers.

09:39.690 --> 09:43.030
But, Chise, what about us?

09:44.600 --> 09:47.020
What are we?

09:50.040 --> 09:52.380
Mages.

09:53.160 --> 09:54.190
That's right.

09:55.220 --> 09:58.610
Had you formed a contract 
of any sort with her?

09:59.700 --> 10:01.120
A contract...

10:05.410 --> 10:07.740
I made a promise.

10:08.460 --> 10:11.140
That we'd make potpourri 
together someday.

10:12.020 --> 10:16.320
Then, as a mage, you'll have 
to uphold that contract.

10:18.660 --> 10:20.670
Ainsworth.

10:20.670 --> 10:22.140
Don't you dare tell me...

10:22.860 --> 10:28.500
So long as we are bound by a contract, 
a mage must act as a mage.

10:29.220 --> 10:31.150
We'll be away for a while.

10:31.560 --> 10:35.260
Nothing good can come of 
spoiling your apprentices.

10:36.510 --> 10:39.870
We're simply following the rules.

10:47.260 --> 10:48.300
Chise?

10:48.300 --> 10:49.850
Mister Ainsworth.

10:50.820 --> 10:52.870
Take me with you, please!

10:52.870 --> 10:54.300
M-Me, too!

10:54.300 --> 10:54.960
And me.

10:55.400 --> 10:57.030
I can't take you all.

10:57.960 --> 11:02.050
The one who killed my family 
ran off with my classmate.

11:02.050 --> 11:05.800
I won't be satisfied until
 I get an answer out of them!

11:06.710 --> 11:09.130
And I can't have her dying now.

11:09.680 --> 11:12.880
We're finally about to 
become venting buddies.

11:12.880 --> 11:15.770
I, er, well...

11:15.770 --> 11:17.310
I'm worried about them.

11:17.310 --> 11:21.020
B-Besides, the only thing 
I can do to help is—

11:21.830 --> 11:23.860
Plotting a coup, are we?

11:24.560 --> 11:26.360
Mister Zaccheroni!

11:26.360 --> 11:27.890
Sounds good to me!

11:27.890 --> 11:31.610
Why not go against the 
grown-ups' orders for once?

11:32.290 --> 11:35.000
I'll tag along if you need some help.

11:35.870 --> 11:37.640
What is your goal?

11:38.100 --> 11:41.150
You get a bonus for good deeds.

11:41.150 --> 11:45.500
More trustworthy than
 an unpaid service, no?

11:47.700 --> 11:49.200
You're right.

11:49.820 --> 11:53.600
In that case, I'm not responsible 
for what happens to any of you.

11:55.290 --> 11:59.440
Hear that? Sir Mage here won't 
protect anyone but his apprentice.

11:59.440 --> 12:04.860
Aspiring sorcerers, you're going to have 
to fend for yourselves as much as you can.

12:04.860 --> 12:08.820
But hey, if it comes to it, 
I'll protect your lives.

12:12.450 --> 12:13.570
Chise?

12:25.550 --> 12:26.860
Florence?

12:33.950 --> 12:34.770
Children...

12:35.790 --> 12:38.940
My brethren, burning in accursed rage...

12:41.670 --> 12:43.940
Crawl, if you cannot fly.

12:44.890 --> 12:46.850
Go to the bottom.

12:48.070 --> 12:51.340
Go, consuming my path of blood.

12:54.430 --> 12:55.440
This is bad.

12:59.970 --> 13:01.110
Lucy!

13:04.670 --> 13:06.000
They're gone.

13:06.560 --> 13:08.810
<i>That's</i> a mage?

13:08.810 --> 13:13.660
There's no way something like 
that is a mere mage.

13:24.490 --> 13:27.540
Yule's just around the corner.

13:27.540 --> 13:30.070
I wish we could get some progress, already.

13:31.900 --> 13:34.250
I've told you so many times.

13:34.690 --> 13:36.040
I don't know when—

13:47.500 --> 13:48.980
Did you see that?

13:48.980 --> 13:50.170
Of course.

13:50.810 --> 13:53.200
I wish I could pretend I didn't.

13:53.200 --> 13:54.540
Should we?

13:54.540 --> 13:55.300
Idiot.

13:55.630 --> 13:58.160
A red dragon on this island...

13:58.940 --> 14:00.710
This is going to be a nightmare.

14:03.110 --> 14:05.600
<i>Follow... follow...</i>

14:06.530 --> 14:08.210
<i>Follow the scent.</i>

14:11.370 --> 14:15.010
<i>Seek out her heart.</i>

14:41.880 --> 14:43.840
You're back, I see.

14:43.840 --> 14:46.610
And you've become quite unsightly.

14:47.510 --> 14:48.710
Philomela.

14:56.640 --> 15:01.440
It seems you've carried out 
your work properly for once.

15:02.220 --> 15:03.890
Grandmother...

15:04.620 --> 15:09.730
Father and Mother will come back now, right?

15:10.320 --> 15:12.360
Both of them, finally...

15:16.420 --> 15:18.070
What I did...

15:18.070 --> 15:23.060
What I did was praiseworthy, wasn't it?

15:29.880 --> 15:34.590
Alcyone, take her underground by sundown.

15:34.590 --> 15:35.650
Right...

15:36.210 --> 15:38.740
You wait outside.

15:38.740 --> 15:42.080
Deal with anyone who 
interferes with the ritual.

15:55.580 --> 15:57.420
Where am I?

16:03.270 --> 16:04.320
Lucy.

16:04.980 --> 16:06.040
Lucy.

16:07.190 --> 16:08.160
Zoe.

16:08.730 --> 16:09.990
Are you all right?

16:10.760 --> 16:12.330
I'm right here, too.

16:12.330 --> 16:13.440
Isaac!

16:13.720 --> 16:18.650
I remember up to being 
swallowed by black liquid...

16:20.490 --> 16:22.540
That's all I remember, too.

16:22.540 --> 16:24.190
Where are we?

16:24.710 --> 16:25.870
The inside.

16:28.560 --> 16:34.820
The only way I could take you with me 
was to bring you inside myself.

16:35.350 --> 16:37.590
Hey, you, mage.

16:37.980 --> 16:40.130
Could you give me a little more space?

16:40.130 --> 16:41.710
I'm stuck.

16:41.710 --> 16:43.950
You're just too big.

16:45.610 --> 16:50.370
So we're on your inside now...

16:50.370 --> 16:51.310
Why?

16:52.020 --> 16:54.080
Because she's moving.

16:54.800 --> 16:56.600
She's on the move.

16:56.600 --> 16:59.730
She seems to be following her scent 
through the underground veins.

17:00.280 --> 17:01.740
Her scent?

17:02.040 --> 17:03.650
The scent of her emotions.

17:03.650 --> 17:05.340
The scent of her soul.

17:05.740 --> 17:09.010
We tend to rely on such things.

17:09.010 --> 17:11.160
You sound like animals.

17:11.160 --> 17:13.200
Humans are animals, too.

17:13.820 --> 17:18.400
But you wouldn't be able to 
dive with us on your own.

17:18.400 --> 17:21.640
So I had to take you inside me.

17:21.640 --> 17:23.150
Underground veins?

17:23.150 --> 17:26.080
There's no way mere humans 
could pass through.

17:26.080 --> 17:28.680
That's no different than going 
directly into the ground.

17:28.680 --> 17:31.400
That's a rule for sorcerers.

17:31.400 --> 17:34.030
There is no such rule for mages.

17:34.670 --> 17:39.340
Though, there aren't many left 
who can do these sorts of things.

17:40.390 --> 17:42.260
What's an underground vein?

17:42.260 --> 17:45.160
An underground passageway for power.

17:45.510 --> 17:47.490
Some are one-way streets.

17:47.490 --> 17:49.320
Some are two-way.

17:49.320 --> 17:51.670
Some are tumultuous, like storms.

17:52.070 --> 17:55.500
Some would say it's pure 
magic power and vitality.

17:55.500 --> 17:59.440
Others theorize that it's 
a mass of organisms.

17:59.440 --> 18:03.500
Big cities often form where 
underground veins pass.

18:05.980 --> 18:07.270
Mother's Back!

18:07.560 --> 18:09.290
Say what?

18:09.290 --> 18:11.900
Oh, it's a phrase from my people's language.

18:11.900 --> 18:16.440
Strings of land where water and trees 
and animals and people gather.

18:16.440 --> 18:19.740
You have the same concept even 
in a different language, huh?

18:20.090 --> 18:24.190
And that silly girl is swimming through 
those parts of the ground, huh?

18:24.840 --> 18:25.770
Yeah.

18:26.460 --> 18:34.200
Mister mage, you lot create magic with the help 
of fairies and sprites and such, don't you?

18:34.570 --> 18:40.560
Whose help did she receive in 
order to become a damn dragon?

18:41.350 --> 18:42.980
A dragon?

18:44.880 --> 18:46.050
We're surfacing.

18:47.270 --> 18:49.760
Magic is never overturned.

18:50.430 --> 18:53.730
So we can think about it later.

19:26.990 --> 19:29.510
All of you, wait here.

19:29.970 --> 19:32.030
I promise I'll come get you out later.

19:33.070 --> 19:33.960
Hold on—

19:33.960 --> 19:36.290
Go out and make eye contact with it now...

19:38.010 --> 19:40.610
and you'll be consumed by 
old maternal instincts.

19:49.270 --> 19:50.790
There you are.

19:51.720 --> 19:56.260
Have you prepared the offering, maiden?

19:57.380 --> 19:59.710
Ms. Lizbeth was right.

19:59.710 --> 20:00.880
We have intruders.

20:01.360 --> 20:03.910
They have quite a bit of magic power.

20:03.910 --> 20:04.960
Sorcerers?

20:05.360 --> 20:08.000
There seem to be several, but 
I can't make a determination.

20:08.000 --> 20:11.360
All I can see is one.

20:11.360 --> 20:13.170
A child with red hair.

20:13.470 --> 20:15.430
No, another one...

20:16.160 --> 20:17.240
A woman?

20:17.770 --> 20:19.140
No, that isn't...

20:19.140 --> 20:20.400
That's...

20:20.790 --> 20:21.990
A...

20:31.050 --> 20:31.750
Hey!

20:32.050 --> 20:32.950
What's wrong?

20:32.950 --> 20:33.770
Hey!

20:34.480 --> 20:36.710
A-A crow!

20:41.320 --> 20:43.220
Lady Philomela...

20:43.760 --> 20:45.290
Will she...

20:45.750 --> 20:50.850
Will Grandmother really bring 
them both back to life?

20:53.260 --> 20:54.880
Alcyone...

20:54.880 --> 20:59.010
Why do I want to have them back?

20:59.800 --> 21:01.170
I...

21:01.670 --> 21:07.980
I don't even remember what 
Mother and Father look like.

21:09.570 --> 21:10.700
But...

21:11.820 --> 21:16.370
But if they come back, I'm sure...

21:16.370 --> 21:20.630
They would praise me, even for what I am.

21:24.610 --> 21:25.750
<i>What shall I do?</i>

21:26.910 --> 21:28.860
<i>What am I to do at a time like this?</i>

21:30.170 --> 21:34.760
<i>What could I possibly do?</i>

21:35.270 --> 21:37.110
<i>I thought I knew...</i>

21:38.330 --> 21:39.370
<i>Something's wrong.</i>

21:39.930 --> 21:41.410
<i>This can't be...</i>

21:49.340 --> 21:54.940
<i>I was certain I'd recorded it.</i>

21:55.890 --> 21:57.450
<i>Ever since then...</i>

22:04.290 --> 22:05.080
Hey.

22:05.510 --> 22:07.410
I'm Adam Sargant.

22:08.000 --> 22:11.440
I'm your master, Alcyone.

22:12.270 --> 22:15.860
I'll leave you in charge of the 
most important task in the world.

22:16.320 --> 22:18.240
Right, Iris?
